  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = (x + 2)^{2} - 25\\). The graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane crosses the \\(x\\)-axis at two points. What is the distance between these two points?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "10"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set \\(f(x) = 0\\): \\((x + 2)^{2} = 25\\), so \\(x + 2 = 5\\) or \\(x + 2 = -5\\).",
    "The \\(x\\)-intercepts are \\(x = 3\\) and \\(x = -7\\).",
    "The distance between \\((3, 0)\\) and \\((-7, 0)\\) is \\(3 - (-7) = 10\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nroots = sorted(solve((x + 2)**2 - 25, x))\nassert roots == [-7, 3]\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == roots[1] - roots[0] == 10",
